| Balance | 1000.00    |

Scenario All dates is what a register with no range chosen shows
Description Stated so that the two cannot drift apart. Choosing All dates
\ after another range puts the register back as it opened, opening
\ balance line and all.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path               | Type     | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking    | Checking | false       |
| Expenses:Groceries | Expense  | false       |
Given today is : Today Vertical
| Date | 2024-05-15 |
Given transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount   | Date       | Payee  | Destination        | Amount  |
| T1  | Assets:Checking | 2022-03-01 | Shop A | Expenses:Groceries | 1000.00 |
| T2  | Assets:Checking | 2024-02-20 | Shop B | Expenses:Groceries | -52.00  |
When register filtered to named range : NamedRangeSelect Vertical
| Name | This year |
When register filtered to named range : NamedRangeSelect Vertical
| Name | All dates |
Then register lines are : RegisterLine CompareOnly
| Ref | Date       | Balance |
| T1  | 2022-03-01 | 1000.00 |
| T2  | 2024-02-20 | 948.00  |
Then opening balance line is : OpeningLine
| AsAt | Balance |
# No rows: there is nothing before the first transaction, so there is no
# opening line at all rather than one reading zero.

Attributes NamedRangeSelect
Description The range the user picked, by name. Since a date carries the date
\ they typed; every other name works its own dates out from today.
| Attribute | Type | Default   |
| Name      | Text |           |
| Since     | Text | none      |

BusinessRule A book may hide everything before a date
Description A book-wide date before which nothing is shown anywhere. It is one
\ setting on the book, and it applies to every register the book opens.
Details This is not the same thing as a named range. A named range is what
\ one register is showing at the moment and the user changes it all
\ day. The hide-before date is a statement about the book -- the
\ years before it were migrated for the record and are not being
\ worked on -- and it is set once in the book's settings.
\
\ Hidden is not deleted and not excluded from arithmetic. The balance
\ brought forward onto the opening line includes every hidden
\ transaction, so the first visible line reads the same balance it
\ read before the date was set, and a report over the hidden years
\ still reports them. Only the register's list is shortened.
\
\ A range the user picks inside the hidden years shows nothing. That
\ is the book's setting winning, which is the point of it being on
\ the book, and the register says why the list is empty rather than
\ looking broken.
\
\ The date is stored on the book's own row, beside the fiscal year
\ start and the check window, so it travels with the book.
Examples: HideBeforeUse
| TheBookSays       | TheUserAsksFor | WhatTheRegisterShows                              |
| Nothing           | All dates      | Everything, as now                                |
| Hide before 2015  | All dates      | 2015 onwards, with the earlier balance brought forward |
| Hide before 2015  | This year      | This year, as it would be anyway                  |
| Hide before 2015  | 2012 to 2013   | Nothing, and a line saying the book hides it      |

Attributes HideBeforeUse
| Attribute            | Type   | Default |
| TheBookSays          | String |         |
| TheUserAsksFor       | String |         |
| WhatTheRegisterShows | String |         |

