| Assets:Checking |
Then blank line is : RegisterLine CompareOnly
| Date       | Payee | Payment | Deposit |
| 2024-05-15 | none  | 0.00    | 0.00    |

Scenario Leaving a part-filled blank line with no amount discards it
Description A payee typed and then thought better of does not become a zero
\ transaction.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path               | Type    | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking    | Checking | false       |
| Expenses:Groceries | Expense | false       |
Given today is : Today Vertical
| Date | 2024-05-15 |
When blank line filled : RegisterLine Vertical CompareOnly
| Payee | Harris Teeter |
When blank line left
Then register lines are : RegisterLine CompareOnly
| Ref |
# No rows: nothing was committed.

Scenario The blank line shows no category and commits to Uncategorized
Description The two halves of the default-destination rule, seen from the
\ register. The empty line at the end is not a transaction, so it
\ shows nothing in the category column -- defaulting there would put a
\ category against a line nobody has entered. Filling in a payee and
\ an amount and leaving the line commits it, and only then is the
\ default applied, because only then is the sign known.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                   | Type     | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking        | Checking | false       |
| Expenses:Uncategorized | Expense  | false       |
Given today is : Today Vertical
| Date | 2024-05-15 |
When register opened on : AccountSelect
| Path            |
| Assets:Checking |
Then blank line is : RegisterLine CompareOnly
| Date       | Category | Payment | Deposit |
| 2024-05-15 | none     | 0.00    | 0.00    |
When blank line filled : RegisterLine Vertical CompareOnly
| Payee   | Harris Teeter |
| Payment | 45.00         |
When blank line left
Then register lines are : RegisterLine CompareOnly
| Date       | Payee         | Category               | Payment | Deposit |
| 2024-05-15 | Harris Teeter | Expenses:Uncategorized | 45.00   | 0.00    |
# See the default-destination rule in Transactions.spectable. The category
# column of the committed line is not blank, and the one above it still is.

Scenario A tag typed on the blank line is kept on the transaction
Description The register has a Tag column, between the memo and the amounts,
\ because the tag is the third thing a transaction says about itself
\ and a column somebody has to open an editor to reach is a column
\ nobody fills in. What is typed is a field of words and every word in
\ it is a tag; see the tag rules in UserInterface.spectable. Nothing
\ completes it here, for the same reason nothing completes the
\ category column here: the two columns behave the same way, which is
\ what the typing rule asks for.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path               | Type     | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking    | Checking | false       |
| Expenses:Groceries | Expense  | false       |
Given today is : Today Vertical
| Date | 2024-05-15 |
When blank line filled : RegisterLine Vertical CompareOnly
| Payee    | Harris Teeter  |
| Category | Expenses:Groceries |
| Tag      | Rental~Kitchen |
| Payment  | 45.00          |
When blank line left
Then register lines are : RegisterLine CompareOnly
| Date       | Payee         | Category           | Tag            | Payment |
| 2024-05-15 | Harris Teeter | Expenses:Groceries | Rental~Kitchen | 45.00   |

Scenario A register line shows the tag the transaction carries
Description Read off the transaction, not worked out: the field is one column on
